===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# To intend to cause harm; to bear malice.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1557|author=[[w:Henry Howard, Earl of Surrey|Henry Howard]]|chapter=Complaint of a lover that defied Love and was by Love after the more tormented|title={{w|Tottel's Miscellany|Songes and Sonettes}}|passage=Thou blinded God (quod I) forgive me this offence, / Unwittingly I went about, to '''malice''' thy pretence.}}
#* {{RQ:Spenser Faerie Queene|year=1596.2|book=VI|canto=IX|page=477|passage=Who on the other ſide did ſeeme ſo farre / From '''malicing''', or grudging his good houre, / That, all he could, he graced him with her, / Ne euer ſhewed ſigne of rancour or of iarre.}}
#* {{RQ:Spenser Fowre Hymnes|page=32|passage=His paines, his pouertie, his ſharpe aſſayes, / Through which he paſt his miſerable dayes, / Offending none, and doing good to all, / Yet being '''maliſt''' both of great and ſmall.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1599|author=w:Ben Jonson|title=w:Every Man out of His Humour|section=act 5, scene 2|passage=I am so far from '''malicing''' their states, / That I begin to pity 'em.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1609|author=w:Samuel Daniel|title=The History of the Civil Wars|others=book 5, verse 48|passage=A feeble spirited king that governed, / Who ill could guide the sceptre he did use; / His enemies, that his worth '''maliced''', / Who both the land and him did much abuse: / The peoples love; and his apparent right, May seem sufficient motives to incite.}}
#* {{quote-song|en|year=1995|author=w:Fugazi|artist=w:Guy Picciotto|title=Fell, Destroyed|album=w:Red Medicine|passage=Here's a list of side effects / Practice tested / Covering every '''maliced''' angle / For example: / You will sleep forever / You will never sleep again}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2005-05-03|title='He was a mess,' woman says of accused|journal=The Whitehorse Star|url=https://www.whitehorsestar.com/News/he-was-a-mess-woman-says-of-accused|passage=Robert Truswell may have been a belligerent and '''malicing''' man, a jury heard this morning during the trial of George Kieran Daunt.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2018-05-14|author=Kimberley Small|quotee=w:Marion Hall|title=Dancehall was contentious, says Marion Hall|journal=The Jamaica Star|url=http://jamaica-star.com/article/entertainment/20180514/dancehall-was-contentious-says-marion-hall|passage=I haven't '''maliced''' anybody, definitely not. I never used to have friends like that. I had a few who I thought were friends. Even if you have friends, things happen and friendship break up, but you move on. But I still talk to everybody.}}

